      "normal_spell_list": {},
      "notes_text": "<table class=\"NormalTable\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"550\">\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">THE GARDEN<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">When you plant a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, it takes root in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">until removed. Your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">is an </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">abstract </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">space whose appearance varies depending on your character's look: it<br>might be a pot on their back, a gap along their blade, or even the ground under their<br>feet. Your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">can only contain </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">one magiseed at a time</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, and any </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseeds </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">in your<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">are </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">automatically removed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">at the end of each scene.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><br></span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">THE GROWTH CLOCK<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">When you acquire the </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Chloromancy </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Skill, you also receive a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Growth Clock </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">which is<br>present </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">only </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">during conflict scenes and represents the cycle of life in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Your Growth Clock has </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">4 sections</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, and it begins each scene </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">empty</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">At the end of your turn, if a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">is present in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">fill 1 section </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">of your<br>Growth Clock; </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">then</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, if there is still a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">and that </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">has<br>an \"at the end of your turn\" effect (see below), apply that effect.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">When you fill the </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">fourth section </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">of your Growth Clock, </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">remove </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">the </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">in your<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, then </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">erase all sections </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">of your Growth Clock.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Sections of your Growth Clock </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">may not be filled nor erased </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">in any way other than<br>described above, through </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Brambleheart </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">and </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Green Thumb </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(pages </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">XXX </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">and </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">XXX</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">), or<br>through effects that </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">explicitly affect Growth Clocks</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><br></span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">MAGISEED EFFECTS<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Magiseeds </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">can have passive effects, or have effects that trigger at the </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">end </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">of your<br>turn, </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">after </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">your Growth Clock has increased.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The effects of a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">magiseed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">apply only while it is present in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">garden</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, and they vary<br>depending on the current number of filled sections in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Growth Clock </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(</span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">T</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">).<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">You </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">only </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">apply the effect corresponding to the </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">exact number </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">of currently filled<br>sections in your </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Growth Clock</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">, not any effect above or below it.<br></span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">w </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">If a magiseed's effect deals damage, it deals 5 extra damage if you are </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">level 30 or<br>higher</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">. If a magiseed's effect causes Hit Point and/or Mind Point loss and/or recovery,<br>the amount increases by 10 if you are </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">level 30 or higher</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "off_attrib_1": "SHI",
      "off_attrib_2": "SHI",
      "off_hand": "",
      "off_hand_attack": "",
      "off_mod_1": "0",
      "off_mod_2": "0",
      "origin": "Sol",
      "passive_list": {
        "0": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">When </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">you fill 1 or more sections of your Growth Clock</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">, you may choose one option:<br>you fill </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">1 additional section </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">of your Growth Clock; </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">or </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">you fill </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">1 fewer section </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">of your<br>Growth Clock (to a minimum of 0 sections filled). </span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">If you do, you cannot use this effect again until after your </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Growth Clock </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">has become completely empty.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br>Additionally, damage dealt by your </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">magiseeds </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">ignores Resistances.</span></p>",
          "passive_name": "GREEN THUMB",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "heroic_skill"
        },
        "1": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">After you use </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Bishop’s Edict </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">or </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">King’s Castle </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Skills, if you are in </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Crisis</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">, you may have every<br>enemy creature present on the scene lose [20] Hit Points.</span></p>",
          "passive_name": "TABULA RASA",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "heroic_skill"
        },
        "2": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">When you acquire this Quirk, write down the <span class=\"fontstyle2\">prophecy</span>, and what it foretold. Do this with the collaboration of everyone else in the group, tie it to a known <span class=\"fontstyle2\">threat or emergency </span>in your world, and describe what <span class=\"fontstyle2\">sign or omen </span>marks you as the person supposedly destined to fulfill that <span class=\"fontstyle2\">prophecy</span>.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">At the end of each session (approximately <span class=\"fontstyle2\">four hours of play</span>), before assigning XP, think <span class=\"fontstyle2\">carefully </span>and <span class=\"fontstyle2\">honestly </span>about what happened during the session and choose <span class=\"fontstyle2\">one </span>of the five options below. The choice is yours to make, but it’s often a good idea to talk about what happened with the rest of the group.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br><span class=\"fontstyle3\">1. </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The prophecy was fulfilled: </span>lose this Quirk, fully restore your Hit Points and Mind Points, recover from all status effects, and gain a Heroic Skill from those available for your Classes (you may even choose a Heroic Skill whose requirements you <span class=\"fontstyle2\">do not </span>satisfy, unless they include a Skill you don’t have).</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br><span class=\"fontstyle3\">2. </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">You acted in accordance to the prophecy: </span>fully restore your Hit Points and Mind Points, and recover from all status effects.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br><span class=\"fontstyle3\">3. </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">You acted neither in accordance to nor against the prophecy: </span>nothing happens.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><span class=\"fontstyle2\">4.You acted against the prophecy: </span>gain 1 Fabula Point.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br><span class=\"fontstyle3\">5. </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The prophecy can never be fulfilled: </span>lose this Quirk, gain 6 Fabula Points, and gain a Heroic Skill from those available for your Classes (you may even choose a Heroic Skill whose requirements you <span class=\"fontstyle2\">do not </span>satisfy, unless they include a Skill you don’t have).<br></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Once the first or last option is chosen, the role of the <span class=\"fontstyle2\">prophecy </span>in your world comes to an end. Even if later on in the campaign it appears that a situation might match the words of the <span class=\"fontstyle2\">prophecy</span>, the effects of this Quirk will no longer be in place: you are free to shape your destiny and act based on your inner moral compass. Or perhaps you always were?</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
          "passive_name": "GLORIOUS FATE",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "quirk"
        },
        "3": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Once before the next rest, after your group makes a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">travel roll</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">, you may </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">reroll the die </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">and keep the new result.</span></p>",
          "passive_name": "Catrography",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp_activity"
        },
        "4": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Once before the next rest, when you lose Hit Points for whatever reason, you may choose to </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">halve <span class=\"fontstyle2\">that HP loss.</span></span></p>",
          "passive_name": "Daydream",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp_activity"
        }
      },
